# Latched emergency stop, served by dyx3_motion_guard (/dyx3/motion_guard/set_emergency_stop).
# Contract: docs/contracts/dyx3_motion_guard.md section 4.

# true asserts the latch; false clears it. Clearing needs this explicit request: the latch
# survives everything except a guard process restart.
bool asserted
# Who is asking. Accepted values (exact, lowercase, compared byte for byte by
# dyx3_motion_guard EstopLatch::request): "tablet", "backend", "ble", "physical".
# Anything else, including an empty string or a different case, is refused with
# REASON_INVALID_SOURCE and changes nothing. Any accepted source may clear a latch asserted by
# another accepted source. The asserting source is echoed in EmergencyStopState.source; it is
# empty while clear.
string source
---
# true only when the latch now holds the requested state. An accepted assert is applied at once:
# the guard runs a decision tick inside the service call, so its next command is STOP, and it
# publishes /dyx3/safety_gate and /dyx3/emergency_stop_state immediately (MG-007).
bool accepted
uint8 REASON_OK=0
uint8 REASON_INVALID_SOURCE=1
uint8 reason_code
